d{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2-8+6 \\\\ -1+10-9 \\\\ 7+2-9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. Since statement ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}=1,\\,{x}_{2}=2$ and ${x}_{3}=3.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275386 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b450f31c-a7d3-5adb-b97f-c4019f0d24ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449768} {:answer/id #uuid "4962641e-6d35-5d45-8933-21ba34104b1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449769}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449769} :answer-field/id #uuid "57cf6e45-5beb-5a14-a281-84a6a9331601" :answer-field/key "$-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450838} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "87325524-6ae2-58a2-8897-92d48ec3d439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449770} {:answer/id #uuid "c96be4f8-7e95-5db6-bfa9-bea58c4af4c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449771}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449770} :answer-field/id #uuid "60cd16bb-e53e-5281-a291-0b77c36d158e" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450839} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84787cf5-8811-58e8-ad22-dae8c976bc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449772} {:answer/id #uuid "e630e0bb-fd55-5de5-aaf8-5cfe405f9675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449773}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449773} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5e69604-33bb-5e80-b406-c41cc964033c" :answer-field/key "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2d5864d3-92dc-56c9-ae91-3d7c6bdd2052" :question/math-academy-id "q-157252" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =-6\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}12-8-4 \\\\ -6+4+2 \\\\ -12+7+5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. Since statement $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}=6,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=1.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-6{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$; “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275387 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8fd2e6-05d0-5b30-963b-06e825131288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449774} {:answer/id #uuid "39c69830-c567-5230-b180-445b08558fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449775}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449774} :answer-field/id #uuid "679e9945-ad45-5f9f-bee3-cbf1a39c8865" :answer-field/key "$-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450841} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65d6efaa-9a84-5e8e-b314-cdea60127cb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449776} {:answer/id #uuid "af932fb4-f3a2-5971-aec5-9759d804797b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449777}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449777} :answer-field/id #uuid "841e39ca-c1bb-52f0-b7a2-17fd3182feb7" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450842} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51338bd6-bb62-534d-8de6-e496d10b0226" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449778} {:answer/id #uuid "51453a9c-1b51-56c2-8aa2-856e4ff4a566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449779}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449779} :answer-field/id #uuid "a474f929-5eb8-5ab7-8b0e-320d9f1b2424" :answer-field/key "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450843}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f4d0dbc3-088e-54a3-8420-9efcf1fc89b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-157253" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+3{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =-\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne \\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 4{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” is true. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is true, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$”; “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55ecca7e-205c-5e10-bf65-d3d1bbcd33f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449780} {:answer/id #uuid "35967e25-346a-5de9-bfb8-8a3dc6109d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449781} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fc873fa-b153-5bb8-a05a-68748c9b661d" :answer-field/key "$4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450844} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9ec9533-e9bc-5548-9ecf-a8025a2dbd0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449782} {:answer/id #uuid "39cfb179-6954-589e-b4f1-69e06c027325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449783}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449782} :answer-field/id #uuid "371913d2-a95b-5a3b-9671-f48a5aa60350" :answer-field/key "${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450845} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b8eeb26-a33b-5553-b0a8-96e77926df4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449784} {:answer/id #uuid "1fbb17c6-439b-53d6-a2ae-4437ffe7bbea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449785}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186449784} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e97e6c-fbd7-5c99-8889-ecf8600edbdf" :answer-field/key "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450846}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2e89e99e-07af-5529-a0c3-3af7fe4158cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-157256" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement $4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =4\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+8{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=4{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement “The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly independent” is false. Since statement “${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$” is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $4{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ only."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284724 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ed1a98b-b70f-5852-93dc-1d3555db439e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.249\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282927} {:answer/id #uuid "b2f8600e-0a44-55b6-b8b1-21dc751c228b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.249\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283242} {:answer/id #uuid "c13c05d3-d6c3-5e3a-a28a-554962580e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.249\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283366} {:answer/id #uuid "e7c9e413-1d81-5c9d-b283-c43e6a6d06f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.429\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283708} {:answer/id #uuid "fb83449b-7ae9-5488-9d93-4529d4997934" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283891}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283366} :answer-field/id #uuid "90796a76-d6ea-589b-8177-e4432db26da3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284180}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "80ffbedc-95be-5629-9877-7afa9025a4f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-17515" :question/problem "![](images/ce/ce8c8d74a7597f04300bf0094826c8245bbd98c45fe8521fec60bada68534f92.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta$ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =1+3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the first quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(3) \\\\  & ≈1.249.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.249$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.249\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c7d3816-389d-5e82-a0f3-ab6f97b998ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281804} {:answer/id #uuid "257797d6-05ee-5418-826e-2dfa1f22a37a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.942\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282017} {:answer/id #uuid "49cc7cc9-242e-5e3c-80c3-3dbc1e84d4f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282315} {:answer/id #uuid "6008122c-e95d-5be2-9259-87ddb71fbe19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=10\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282502} {:answer/id #uuid "78f026be-5b0d-5012-87c5-403387261c1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282723}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282315} :answer-field/id #uuid "349fe9ca-9819-5814-bf38-b0878226c548" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "66528dcf-b6ba-5409-902c-695b0a7a762c" :question/math-academy-id "q-17516" :question/problem "![](images/f1/f13d134b7dba012b5b71a7a81ab8071b2706586699b8bf21a6df0d5c44c69619.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta$ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =3-\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)| \\\\  & ≈5.961.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =5.961$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.961\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43655d54-a035-536e-a010-bd443029e007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.434\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282264} {:answer/id #uuid "72f2fc7b-2c6f-5985-85a5-e5bb36010224" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282673} {:answer/id #uuid "7606b361-6884-59ff-828e-65e8c776f5ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.857\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282698} {:answer/id #uuid "826ba727-3106-57fa-ac84-669284823289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.927\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282812} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd0266d-1e94-52e9-858b-e3399750f227" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.927\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283504}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282673} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fbc9f8b-5f4d-53b3-a743-b65e32e917f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c203d292-6345-5970-9cf8-807d3fcdd74d" :question/math-academy-id "q-17519" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-4-3\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta$ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)| \\\\  & ≈\\pi +0.643\\,50… \\\\  & ≈3.785.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=5$ and $\\theta =3.785$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.785\\,\\text{i}}\\,.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284727 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46f6cb0e-eb17-577e-aecc-4807b65d3847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.678\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282288} {:answer/id #uuid "68f5722b-68d2-58ea-92a2-f8e8876cfcdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.786\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282588} {:answer/id #uuid "70afd270-92c3-5b3b-8843-b8550be52a24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.678\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282653} {:answer/id #uuid "96311d46-c230-5b88-845e-4f2305873343" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282986} {:answer/id #uuid "fd434491-ebfe-53d7-93e6-0e34ad9bacb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283909}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282288} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0af69bc-a1ef-5f95-89c7-a4c975fad283" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7369e709-362c-5373-8931-5b866971acf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-17521" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-4+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta$ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)| \\\\  & ≈2.678.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =2.678$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{2.678\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21aa4008-d8d1-557e-a8a5-b050d042158f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=5\\,{\\text{e}}^{3\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281987} {:answer/id #uuid "41fa998e-0c28-5431-a98a-fd2785313841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282254} {:answer/id #uuid "61f95004-13b8-532c-bc01-e3b2fdab54a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282523} {:answer/id #uuid "6619876c-f2d2-5661-8e43-a021a536b03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282570} {:answer/id #uuid "832f33f1-8fad-5036-8eb4-c5a4a3ff4aeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282823}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282570} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf4a68b-3d5d-5aee-8879-b9de12d1f208" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284354}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "6769607e-a98e-55fe-a42b-31c1a377dfe6" :question/math-academy-id "q-17523" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-3-3\\text{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the third quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{y}{x}\\right)| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\left(\\frac{-3}{-3}\\right)| \\\\  & =\\pi +|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1)| \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=3\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=3\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5\\pi \\text{i}/4}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284729 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82522bd6-f84a-5cc4-addb-e65da105a963" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.389\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282810} {:answer/id #uuid "aac0b3aa-deb5-598a-9d4f-2d39c14fe30f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283169} {:answer/id #uuid "b71c8aab-0b52-56ba-a243-113c5f24279a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283274} {:answer/id #uuid "cb6d7ba8-0f0