true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477244}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186477244} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ef61896-29e1-5706-91a7-6ea55283ff0f" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477591}] [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e01fd7c0-afad-5c3d-b6da-dc32877f541a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477245} {:answer/id #uuid "8be6cd95-0040-5363-af7f-8b2704b626e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477246}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186477245} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fc6a235-aad1-5564-825b-64bf12cd21c1" :answer-field/key "The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477592}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14d3b9a6-b42e-5d81-b5e8-d7e65c357f71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510826} {:answer/id #uuid "5a089876-2b6c-5a99-9e81-d189370977ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510972} {:answer/id #uuid "6e02d051-6b0a-5a1c-8d4f-65d665e53a26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511009} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e669dd-ebc9-5d9b-a6c3-bf1f63c51806" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511150} {:answer/id #uuid "d63d1670-ebb4-54f4-afea-a48835538de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511221}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511150} :answer-field/id #uuid "993bd62a-640e-5656-8035-d20d8bad796e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "6d3ae80f-587f-5674-9679-5efb33bf0d2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-157227" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =-3\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-12+0+2 \\\\ 3+6+4 \\\\ 0+0+10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne \\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNotice that we can reorder the equations in this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system using back substitution, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is true, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564481 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04f0f6d1-8402-5397-ac16-a4b89f34b7f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563978} {:answer/id #uuid "19a0357a-ce57-58ed-bfb1-8181d4484baa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564004} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc05134-02b1-5727-8502-07a1f3d7d9e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564041} {:answer/id #uuid "35f96482-abb5-57cb-8ffa-3db8da48fb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564057} {:answer/id #uuid "de9cfaf8-1939-5e03-9914-e2205bc5fb25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564321}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563978} :answer-field/id #uuid "d31dd379-95e8-5e67-883a-a09641f1eecc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "34925275-ae4c-5d65-95f3-737bbc060369" :question/math-academy-id "q-75642" :question/problem "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${\\mathbf{a}}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}=2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=2{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-2{\\mathbf{a}}_{1} & =\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+(-1){\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564487 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b93e02-911f-5448-ab37-cc2c74c1efa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563983} {:answer/id #uuid "2aa4ebb0-8d31-5131-bf0e-7bb725b939ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564035} {:answer/id #uuid "3fe615b5-1980-5ec3-8f2a-a28dfe3cf0c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564078} {:answer/id #uuid "466b980c-756d-5db4-8e7c-797a12ae9d1a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "None of the statements are true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564086} {:answer/id #uuid "e608ec51-2291-5759-a881-171cd19404a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564329}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563983} :answer-field/id #uuid "11e59e1d-92dd-58fa-bf22-f25988693e4e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "5873b1df-0474-5771-9ef7-dcd0b294d997" :question/math-academy-id "q-105317" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 20 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nII. The vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nIII. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ has an infinite number of nonzero solution." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2},$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+20{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-13{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 20 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -13 & 0\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -1 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 0\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+2(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-(\\mathbf{0})+9(\\mathbf{0})=\\mathbf{0}\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$, we get that the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are false, while statement II is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564502 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0248fac4-7021-5d3c-8fe6-630d74a3d1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563972} {:answer/id #uuid "2d59668a-5b18-5b17-be7f-d90767135530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564044} {:answer/id #uuid "a19b5317-af1f-54a5-aa91-38cce6394e14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564214} {:answer/id #uuid "de17d5bf-c3c6-5996-a382-6447bcc6e98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564319} {:answer/id #uuid "e5988f07-d1dc-55e6-8850-b106bbc457fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564328}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564044} :answer-field/id #uuid "e84dcffa-6797-50d5-aaea-ce1046d2837d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "848dcb43-d675-54a9-ae47-a5c4f5dfb881" :question/math-academy-id "q-157254" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-2{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -21\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne \\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The equation ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0} \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2} &=\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving this system, we find that the solution is ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2}.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a561db8-da05-5488-90b2-b1499bdfd024" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563985} {:answer/id #uuid "14137556-54c3-5d40-a07b-5a7c1bb6e3a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563998} {:answer/id #uuid "62097d8f-b2fe-5ff4-a7b0-e3bbc5636bd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564121} {:answer/id #uuid "68f85d0f-2150-5cfc-8c7b-b48fb1678f4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564134} {:answer/id #uuid "8df14e3b-06f0-5de6-a3f3-c95b09e3bf3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564190}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564134} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd435012-1099-531b-992e-08104da3eb22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "de9e1bb6-8c29-536b-b329-05255b6d1f04" :question/math-academy-id "q-75636" :question/problem "The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}\\}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${\\mathbf{a}}_{2}$ if\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer is \n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTo see why, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}=-3\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThis way, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1} & =\\mathbf{0} \\\\ 3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{\\mathbf{a}}_{2} & =\\mathbf{0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the vectors ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{2}$ are parallel.\n\nTo see why this means that ${\\mathbf{a}}_{1}$ and ${\\mathbf{a}}_{2}$ are linearly dependent, we notice that the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nhas the solution ${x}_{1}=3$ and ${x}_{2}=1,$ which is different from ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Therefore, the set is linearly dependent."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572667 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "123e6b37-f5d0-58a4-a315-71252699ea45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572335} {:answer/id #uuid "3781813b-d8b2-5b24-921b-dce30178d1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572381} {:answer/id #uuid "49b8843e-8d82-574e-a9c8-a640d411e4e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572405} {:answer/id #uuid "7217c7fb-bda2-5564-844d-cd64e72c50f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572447} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f980f5-230b-530c-bbfe-2be36a54ca2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572550}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186572405} :answer-field/id #uuid "24809e24-c6b5-5bd7-a31f-2f0864640659" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572601}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0bcf3acb-d9f4-5535-b8d1-de8e7ee2e9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-157235" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nII. ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ only if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$\n\nIII. The set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly dependent." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${\\mathbf{v}}_{1},{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}$ and ${\\mathbf{v}}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{v}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{v}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{v}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}-{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+2{\\mathbf{a}}_{3} & =3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6-4-2 \\\\ 9+5-14 \\\\ -3+3+0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\mathbf{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since statement I is true, we have ${x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{1}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{2}+{x}_{3}{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}=\\mathbf{0}$ for ${x}_{1}=3,\\,{x}_{2}=-1$ and ${x}_{3}=2.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since statement II is false, the set $\\{{\\mathbf{a}}_{1},{\\mathbf{a}}_{2},{\\mathbf{a}}_{3}\\}$ is linearly *dependent*.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""}]}
